<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97208" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στριφνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>firm, hard, solid</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				15
			</span></i> cod. M (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρυφν-</span> cett.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκες -ότεραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.111
				</span></i>
			 (codd. boni, 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρυφν-</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nat.Mul.</u>
				1
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στριφρ-, στρυφν-</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ὁ ἐγκέφαλος συνέστηκε καί ἐστι
				στριφνός</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιφρός, στρυφνός</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέρμα ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.642e
			</span></i> codd.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστέα στριφνότατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Carn.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρυφν-</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ἀλεκτρυὼν μάλα ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Epit.</u>
				168
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρὴ ς. τ᾽ ἐκτάδιός
			τε</span>, 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρυφνή</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.411
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στριφνός</span> is Hellenistic
			for 
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιφρός</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Moer.
				p.342
			</span></i> P., cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gloss. Oxy.</u>
				1803.1
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στριφνός</span>
			=
			<i>acerbus</i> (leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρυφνός</span>),
				<u>Gloss.</u>; also =
			<i>rigidus</i> and <i>strigosus</i>, ibid.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στριφνοὶ γέροντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					180
				</span></i>
			 (as cited by <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στριφνούς</span>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεριφνοί</span> codd.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιπτοί</span> codd. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i>).</div>
